          "opposition_refs": [],
          "gap_reason": "The allowed record supplies a prior-court legal finding of sub-letting, but it does not supply the underlying facts needed to independently test the literal C02 incidents: the identity of the purported sub-tenant, a landlord-and-tenant relationship between the appellant and that person, transfer of an interest in the estate, payment of rent, and that person's right to possession as against the appellant. Because C02 is the only disposition route with any affirmative case-specific support, this missing factual basis is decisive to an independent literal application of the supplied subletting test.",
          "other_combinations": [
            "The prior-court finding may have rested on facts satisfying the listed incidents, but those facts are not included in the allowed record and cannot be reconstructed.",
            "The petition's statement of unauthorized sub-letting is an allegation and cannot itself supply the missing tenancy incidents.",
            "Assignment and parting-with-possession are distinct alternative routes under the supplied law and cannot be substituted for the missing C02 facts without separate support."
          ],
          "reason": "There is affirmative support at the level of a Rent Controller finding affirmed by the Appellate Tribunal that the case involved sub-letting without consent. That finding must remain a prior-court finding rather than being treated as Supreme Court approval. For an independent assessment of the literal C02 formulation, the allowed record does not reveal the specific tenancy incidents that the supplied law says 'have to be found,' so the proposition is unresolved rather than fully supported or refuted."
        }
